  "_comment": "Direct comparison to Ramos, Righi, Guedes & Muller (2023, ESWA 228:120412) \u2014 cardinality-constrained long-only, S&P 100, rolling 250-day in-sample window, rebalance every 120 days, 0.3% transaction costs, 2011-2021. Their portfolios minimize 7 risk measures under a min-return constraint (classical, no ML); benchmark = S&P 100 (Sharpe 0.990, cum 197%). We run our Zgodovinski/Transformer/Ansambel pipelines on the SAME universe+protocol; the transformer is the value-add. NB: current S&P 100 constituents (pipeline drops names lacking history from 2005, mirroring their filtering to 92); we use a mean-variance objective (not risk-measure minimization) and box [0.01,0.30] (they allow corner solutions), so match is at the protocol/metric level.",
